        "original_id": "8e572ff4-0265-50c4-ad7b-17330cf3d774",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Franklin Pierce, Lewis Cass, Baw Breese\n- Events: 1852 Democratic National Convention, Indian removal\n- Roles: American military officer, United States Senator, treaty signer\n- Places: Michigan, United States\n\nFacts:\n- At the 1852 Democratic National Convention, Franklin Pierce was nominated over Lewis Cass.\n- Lewis Cass was an American military officer who represented Michigan in the United States Senate.\n- Lewis Cass signed a treaty on behalf of the United States that outlined voluntary Indian emigration.\n- The Indian emigration described in that treaty was later made mandatory and enforced by the military.\n- Baw Breese was forcibly removed during that period of Indian removal.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
